course: dictionary
lesson: 11999
title: A special feature
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A characteristic is a special quality or feature that helps you tell one thing or person from another. Look at the clues around the word: «Stripes are a characteristic of tigers.» Stripes are something tigers have that helps you know a tiger when you see one.
explain: Characteristic can also be an adjective, meaning typical of someone or something. «She gave her characteristic smile.» If she always smiles this way, the smile is typical of her. Ask yourself: is this how they usually are? If so, characteristic fits.
explain: You will meet characteristic in science, maths and stories. In science we sort animals by their characteristics, such as fur or wings. In maths, a triangle has three sides and three corners, and those are its characteristics. To check a meaning, swap in «typical feature» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Characteristic (noun) means a special quality or feature that helps you tell things apart.
fact: Characteristic (adjective) means typical of someone or something.
fact: «Physical characteristics» means features you can see or measure, like height, hair colour or the shape of a body.
fact: The phrase «a characteristic of» is useful: «Fur is a characteristic of mammals.»
fact: The plural is characteristics: «Legs, fur and wings are characteristics of animals.»
exercise: «Stripes are a characteristic of tigers.» What is a characteristic? | A loud noise made by a cat | A place where tigers sleep | *A special feature that helps you tell one thing from another | A type of food tigers eat
exercise: «Her characteristic smile made everyone feel welcome.» What does characteristic mean here? | Hidden under a hat | Angry and loud | *Typical of her | Sleepy and slow
exercise: «A triangle has three sides and three corners; these are its characteristics.» Which is a characteristic of a triangle? | *Three sides | Round edges | Four equal sides | Soft fur
test: «Physical characteristics» means what? | Feelings you hide from other people | Rules about school sports | Sounds that animals make | *Features you can see or measure, like height or hair colour
test: «The dog's characteristic bark is loud and deep.» What does characteristic mean here? | Quiet | *Typical of the dog | Broken | Hidden
exam: In «Long ears are a characteristic of rabbits», which word could you swap in for characteristic? | Shadow | Hobby | Mistake | *Feature
